course: dictionary
lesson: 11642
title: Money owed and late
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Arrears is a money word. It means money that is owed and should have been paid already. «The family was three months in arrears with their rent.» The clues are owed and should have been paid already, so arrears must mean late money that is still owing.
explain: You will almost always see arrears in its plural form, even for a small amount. Look for the phrases: rent arrears, fall into arrears and pay off the arrears. «Mia paid off her arrears in June.» To pay off arrears means to pay all the late money at last.
explain: Be careful with «paid in arrears». This does not mean the money is late. It means the money is paid at the end of a period of work, not at the start. «Jo is paid in arrears, so she gets her wages on the last day of the month.» Check by swapping in your meaning: "paid at the end" still makes sense.
fact: Arrears means money that is owed and should have been paid already.
fact: «In arrears» means late with payments that are owed.
fact: «Rent arrears» means rent that is owed and not yet paid.
fact: «Paid in arrears» means paid at the end of a period of work, not at the start.
fact: Arrears is a formal word, so you will see it in letters, news and money problems.
exercise: «Dad fell into arrears with the electricity bill.» What does arrears mean here? | Money saved in a jar | Money given away as a present | A small bill that is always paid on time | *Money owed that should have been paid already
exercise: «Lee is paid in arrears, so he gets his wages at the end of the month.» When is Lee paid? | Only on his birthday | Never | *At the end of the work period | At the very start, before he works
exercise: Which phrase means late with payments that are owed? | in advance | *in arrears | spare change | paid in full
test: «The club wants the arrears paid off this week.» What does pay off the arrears mean? | Give the club a present | Close the club for good | *Pay all the late money that is owed | Count the members in the hall
test: Mum says «we are in arrears with the water bill». What does this mean? | We have a very large amount of water | We have paid the water bill early | We have no water bill at all | *We owe money that is late
exam: «Sam paid the arrears on his phone bill, so he owes nothing now.» What does arrears mean in this sentence? | The phone's battery | A new phone bill that is not yet due | Extra money paid for a gift | *Money owed that was late
